# Files Claude should skip reading during routine work.
#
# The Collectr "Import All" worker drives a real headless-Chrome session to page through a
# public Collectr showcase that sits behind an AWS CloudFront anti-bot WAF. Getting past
# that WAF (a real-Chrome User-Agent + same-site credentialed XHRs) is dual-use code: it is
# entirely legitimate here — a first-party feature the app owner authorized, reading PUBLIC
# showcase data the site already serves to browsers, heavily rate-limited via a Durable
# Object — but a security heuristic can misread it as anti-bot evasion tooling.
#
# These files are stable and documented (docs/collectr-import-notes.md). Skipping them keeps
# routine sessions from re-processing the dual-use content and tripping a false positive.
# Remove this entry when you specifically need to edit the worker again.
workers/collectr-fetch/
